Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.45,Cap,,0,0,0,,My name is Mitch, and\NI want to tell you
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.47,0:00:04.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,about the thing that\Nvisited me after
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.75,0:00:07.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,I moved into my\Nbrother's house.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.02,0:00:09.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,I used to call ghosts\Nnonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.25,0:00:11.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then something climbed\Nthrough my
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.24,0:00:13.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,window with empty\Nblack eyes, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.22,0:00:15.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,I never called it\Nnonsense again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.65,0:00:17.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let us go back to the\Nbeginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.78,0:00:20.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,A week after my own\Nhouse was foreclosed,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.44,0:00:22.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,I moved in with my\Nbrother Edwin.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.87,0:00:24.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,We had not spoken in\Nten years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.92,0:00:26.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,so I was glad to be\Nthere.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.94,0:00:28.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,The first night I fell\Nasleep
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.88,0:00:30.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,fast, happy for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.74,0:00:32.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,Around one in the\Nmorning I heard
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.81,0:00:34.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,rustling outside my\Nwindow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.80,0:00:36.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,Something scratched\Nslowly
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.21,0:00:37.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,against the glass\Npane.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.76,0:00:40.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,I told myself it was\Nonly a raccoon
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.06,0:00:41.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,and went back to\Nsleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.88,0:00:44.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the morning I\Nmentioned it to Edwin,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.15,0:00:46.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,and he agreed it was\Nprobably nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.82,0:00:49.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,The next night I woke\Nto my window sliding
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.60,0:00:52.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,open, then a heavy\Nthump on the floor,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.11,0:00:54.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,as if something had\Nclimbed inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.72,0:00:55.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,I searched the room,\Nbut
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.98,0:00:57.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,I saw nothing there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.33,0:00:59.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the morning Edwin\Ndropped his coffee
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.85,0:01:02.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,cup the moment he saw\Nmy face.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.08,0:01:03.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,He held up a mirror.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.64,0:01:06.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,A long gash had opened\Nacross my left cheek
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.36,0:01:09.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,overnight, and I had\Nno memory of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.15,0:01:11.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,At the hospital the\Ndoctor lifted my
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.36,0:01:13.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,shirt to show me a\Nfresh, sewn incision
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.74,0:01:15.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,where a kidney should\Nhave been.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.00,0:01:18.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,He told me I had\Nsomehow lost it in the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.40,0:01:20.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,night, and that he did\Nnot know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.92,0:01:22.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,I could not answer\Nhim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.71,0:01:25.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,On the third night I\Nwoke at midnight
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.15,0:01:27.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,to a creature leaning\Nover my bed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.39,0:01:30.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,a dark hoodie pulled\Nlow, a cracked blue
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.03,0:01:32.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,mask with no mouth and\Nno nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.37,0:01:34.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,Where its eyes should\Nhave been there
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.55,0:01:36.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,was only black, empty\Nsockets, with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.60,0:01:38.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,a black fluid dripping\Nfrom them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.99,0:01:41.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,It lunged for my chest\Nwith long pale
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.53,0:01:43.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,fingers, clawing for\Nmy ribs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.82,0:01:45.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,I grabbed the camera\Nfrom the mantel
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.01,0:01:48.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,and took one picture\Nbefore I kicked
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.21,0:01:50.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,it hard in the face\Nand ran.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.22,0:01:52.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,I fled into the dark\Nwoods behind
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.22,0:01:54.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,the house, until I\Ntripped on a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.10,0:01:56.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,rock and everything\Nwent black.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.43,0:01:58.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,I woke again in a\Nhospital bed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.66,0:02:00.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,with only minor\Ninjuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.82,0:02:03.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,The doctor said my\Nparents were coming
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.08,0:02:05.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,for me, and then his\Nface changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.39,0:02:06.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,My brother, he told\Nme, had
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.00,0:02:08.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,been killed by\Nsomething.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.79,0:02:10.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,I am sorry, Mitch, he\Nsaid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.76,0:02:12.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,My parents drove me\Nback
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.15,0:02:13.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,to gather my things.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.62,0:02:15.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the hallway lay\NEdwin's body,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.58,0:02:17.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,and beside it\Nsomething small.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.72,0:02:20.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,I picked it up without\Ntelling them what
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.05,0:02:22.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,I had found, and in\Nthe car I finally
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.21,0:02:24.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,looked down at what I\Nwas holding.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.49,0:02:26.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was wrapped in dark\Ncloth, cold
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.67,0:02:28.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,and wet with that\Nblack fluid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.89,0:02:31.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,It was the piece taken\Nfrom my side,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.16,0:02:33.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,half-eaten and still\Nwarm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.24,0:02:35.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,This story is inspired\Nby the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.21,0:02:37.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,Eyeless Jack\Ncreepypasta, shared
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.38,0:02:39.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,online in twenty\Ntwelve.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.46,0:02:40.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.72,0:02:41.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have\Nbelieved
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.88,0:02:42.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,it was only a raccoon?
